ction  short-term and unsustainable regimes  most people who have the dieting mindset  tend to gain more weight over time let  me know in the comments below if you  have dieted before  so ditch dieting and change that to  healthy eating instead focus on  nourishing your body instead of  depriving it and be mindful of your  eating habits watch this video right  here and learn how you can lose weight  without eating less most of the time we  tend to overeat because we're not aware  of our hunger and appetite we eat until  we're absolutely stuffed and sometimes  we're not even aware of the food we've  eaten if i were to ask you right now to  think back of all the meals and snacks  you have eaten today  can you list them down how did you feel  while eating were you truly hungry how  did you feel afterwards satisfied or  guilty i've also filmed a video on the 8  types of hunger which you can watch and  learn more about your own eating habits  once you're able to eat and stop when  your body feels about 80 full you'll  realize that eating healthily and  mindfully is not that difficult  and this habit will help you to keep  your weight off for good and maintain a  healthy weight for life  our goal primarily is to become fitter  healthier and happier person from the  inside and out  what if i told you that shedding those  ponds can be as easy as engaging in a  little spring cleaning well it's true  the new year is a good time to spring  clean and organize your pantry this is a  perfect opportunity to create a clean  slate of food supply at home so remove  all processed and junk food from your  home that aren't helping you to lose  weight replace them with fresh natural  food if you store junk food at home  chances are you will eat them if you  stock up on fresh natural food similarly  you are more likely to eat them i mean  just think about it if you have cookies  out on your kitchen counter chances are  you will snack on them  instead replace them with healthier  snacks su